=== P2 Shared surface 0159 SortControl (Windows) ===

SURFACE: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/SortControl.{cs,Model.cs,Source.cs,ViewModel.cs}
WEB SOURCE: web/src/components/forms/SortControl.tsx  (field dropdown + direction toggle, controlled)
TESTS: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/SortControlTests.cs (41 headless test cases)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Composition: the web source renders [field <Select>] + [direction <button>] in an inline flex row
  (gap-1). The native surface mirrors that with a horizontal StackPanel (Spacing=4) hosting the shared
  Components/UI TsSelect (the native counterpart of web @/components/ui/Select) followed by an Icon-variant
  TsButton direction toggle. NOT a hand-rolled control - it composes the shared primitives per Windows HIG.
- Data sources (web hooks -> native seams): the ONLY web hook is useTranslation -> ILocalizer (P1/S10). The
  web component is fully CONTROLLED - field / direction / options / directionAriaLabel are props the parent
  owns and onFieldChange / onDirectionChange callbacks report changes. The native ISortControlSource (P1/S8
  seam) plays the parent's role: it holds the state and raises Changed (re-projection) plus the specific
  FieldChanged / DirectionChanged events (web callbacks). The view performs no I/O.
- Shared components used (web @/components/ui/Select) -> native Components/UI TsSelect (ComboBox-based,
  DisplayMemberPath="Label"); the direction toggle is the shared Components/UI TsButton (Icon variant). The
  direction enum reuses the shared Core TeslaSync.App.Core.SortDirection (DRY; the same enum + ChevronUp/Down
  glyphs TsDataTable already uses for column sort), normalized to a strict ascending/descending two-state.
- States reproduced (every branch the web source actually renders):
    * ascending  -> ChevronUp glyph (web ArrowUp) + "Ascending" label/tooltip (web direction === 'asc').
    * descending -> ChevronDown glyph (web ArrowDown) + "Descending" label/tooltip.
    * populated  -> the field dropdown bound to the options with the selected field resolved to its label.
    * empty      -> when the option set is empty the field picker renders LABELED + DISABLED (never a blank
                    box); the web would render an empty <select>, so disabling is a strict native improvement
                    that invents no copy and no new i18n key.
  The web SortControl is a CONTROLLED, presentational form control with no query-freshness or connectivity
  concept, so it has NO loading / error / stale / offline chrome - and none is invented (honesty covenant:
  no drift in either direction; same reasoning the predecessor Combobox/Delta surfaces logged).
- Behaviour parity: picking a field -> source.SetField (web onFieldChange); clicking the toggle flips
  ascending <-> descending and swaps the arrow glyph (web flip / onDirectionChange, L51). Programmatic
  selection sync is re-entrancy guarded so the projection never feeds back into onFieldChange.
- i18n (web t() keys -> P1/S10): the 4 sortControl.* keys did NOT exist in the catalog, so they were ADDED to
  Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (4/4 each, verified):
    sortControl.ascending "Ascending" | sortControl.descending "Descending" |
    sortControl.fieldLabel "Sort by"  | sortControl.direction "Sort direction".
  ar/he are seeded with the English value, matching the established catalog precedent (the combobox/avatar
  keys are English-seeded in ar/he pending localization). No English literals in native code; every visible
  string flows through the localizer + SortControlRegistration fallbacks (verbatim from the web second args).
- Accessibility: the field dropdown carries the localized "Sort by" Narrator name (web aria-label); the
  direction toggle carries the localized "Sort direction: {Ascending|Descending}" name (web aria-label, with
  the explicit directionAriaLabel override honored verbatim) + the direction label as its tooltip (web title);
  the arrow glyph is the visible direction indicator. Inherits WinUI hover/pressed/focus visuals, Narrator
  support and system font scaling from TsButton/TsSelect. No animation -> reduced-motion is a non-issue.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): emits `view.opened slug=SortControl` once on Loaded. PII-safe (slug only; never the
  selected field, the direction, or any option label - asserted by a leak test).

